# .image-version-ignore — files whose `ghcr.io/vibeic/vibeic-eda:X.Y.Z` mentions
# are HISTORY, not live install pointers, so the drift-net must not flag them
# when VERSION advances. One glob per line (matched against basename AND repo-rel
# path; see sync_image_version.py::_matches). HISTORY_GLOBS already covers
# FIX_STATUS / CHANGELOG / *ROADMAP* / *_STATUS.md.
#
# Benchmark RESULT.md files record WHICH image a PAST clean-room run used (its
# tool-substitution disclosure). That tag is an immutable record of that run —
# never a live pointer that should track VERSION — so ignore them.
RESULT.md
# Sign-off reports are the same: they record the exact toolchain a SPECIFIC
# tapeout/sign-off run used (e.g. a commercial-PDK SPM sign-off on 0.2.16 / yosys 0.66-vibeic).
# 0.2.17 ships yosys 0.67, so bumping the tag would misstate that run — history.
*SIGNOFF*.md

# A benchmark RUN RECORD, not a live install pointer: it states which image
# that run actually used (0.2.20). Rewriting it to the current VERSION would
# falsify the record rather than fix a stale doc — same reason a gatekeeper
# run log is never retroactively edited.
benchmark-data/ic/caravel_user_project/clean_run_v1432int_commercial/SOURCE_MANIFEST.md

# Provenance measurement notes, NOT live install pointers: each records the
# EXACT image the gf180 PDK asset globs were VERIFIED against (0.2.24). The PDK
# assets are identical across EDA-image versions, so the globs stay valid, but
# bumping the tag would FALSELY claim re-verification against a newer image —
# a measurement-honesty violation. Left as the historical 0.2.24 record.
vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/programs/pdk_registry.json
vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/programs/tests/test_gf180_registry_assets_resolve.py
